# Privacy Policy for CubeTicTacToe

**Last updated: April 28, 2026**

This Privacy Policy explains how CubeTicTacToe ("the App", "we", "us") collects, uses, and protects your information when you use our mobile game.

## 1. Information We Collect

To enable online multiplayer and leaderboards, the App collects the following information through Firebase services provided by Google:

### Account Information (via Firebase Authentication)
- Email address
- Unique user ID (Firebase UID)
- Display name (nickname) you choose
- Profile picture (only if you sign in with Google)

### Gameplay Data (via Firebase Realtime Database / Firestore)
- Match results, scores, and ranking information
- Game session data required for online multiplayer
- Nickname displayed to other players on leaderboards

### Technical Data (via Firebase, optional)
- Crash reports (Firebase Crashlytics) to improve app stability
- Basic device information for troubleshooting

We do **not** collect:
- Your real name, phone number, or address
- Your location
- Your contacts, photos, or files
- Any payment information (no in-app purchases)
- Advertising identifiers (no advertising in this app)

## 2. How We Use Your Information

We use the collected information solely to:
- Authenticate your account and enable login
- Match you with other players for online multiplayer games
- Display your rank and nickname on the leaderboard
- Maintain and improve app stability through crash reports

We do **not** sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.

## 3. Data Storage and Security

- All data is stored on Google Firebase servers, which use industry-standard encryption.
- Data is transmitted over HTTPS (encrypted in transit).
- Your password is never stored by us; Firebase handles authentication securely.

## 4. Third-Party Services

The App uses the following Google Firebase services:
- **Firebase Authentication** — for account login
- **Firebase Realtime Database / Firestore** — for multiplayer and leaderboards
- **Firebase Crashlytics** (if used) — for crash reporting

For information on how Google handles data, see Google's Privacy Policy:
https://policies.google.com/privacy

## 5. Your Rights and Choices

You have the right to:
- **Access** the data we hold about you
- **Delete** your account and all associated data
- **Correct** inaccurate information (e.g., change your nickname)

### How to Delete Your Account and Data
You can delete your account at any time:
1. **In-app**: Go to Settings → Account → Delete Account
2. **Or by email**: Send a deletion request to the email below

When you delete your account, all your personal data (email, UID, nickname, match history, leaderboard records) will be permanently removed within 30 days.

## 6. Children's Privacy

The App is intended for users aged 13 and older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can remove it.

## 7. International Data Transfers

Firebase servers may be located outside your country. By using the App, you consent to the transfer of your information to these servers, which are protected by Google's security standards.

## 8. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Significant changes will be announced within the App or on this page. The "Last updated" date will reflect the most recent revision.

